[size=5][b]Bulk Sell Equipment[/b][/size]
Finds the appraised talismans you no longer need and sells them all at once. It works the same way the game's [b]View/Sell Equipment[/b] screen does, with the same price and the same game calls.

This version sells [b]appraised talismans only[/b] (Unknown / Historical / Secret / Golden Age Charm, rarity 5-8). Weapons, armor and crafted talismans are never touched.

[b]New here?[/b] Read the [url=https://github.com/zamcoder/bulk-sell-equipment-mhwilds/blob/main/docs/GUIDE.md]beginner's guide[/url]: your first sale in 6 steps, which Keep option to choose, how to read the window, and short recipes with examples.

[size=4][b]How it decides[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Default[/b]: only duplicates, and talismans that a talisman you keep matches or beats on every skill and slot.
[*][b]More space[/b]: choose [b]Keep the best 3 per skill[/b] (or 10, 5, 2, 1). For every skill and every slot shape, your 3 best talismans stay; every other unique talisman up to your rarity limit is sold. The [b]Skills[/b] panel changes this per skill.
[*][b]Your control[/b]: tick or untick any row; your choice beats the rules. [b]Mark shown[/b] ticks every row a filter shows, with Undo.
[*][b]The promise[/b]: the rules never lower your best level of any skill, and never remove the last talisman that can hold a slot shape. Only your own ticks and Don't care settings can, and the confirmation names exactly what you lose.
[/list]
[size=4][b]How "Keep the best N per skill" works[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Protected talismans stay[/b] (see below). Your own ticks come next: a ticked row is sold, an unticked one is kept.
[*][b]Duplicates and covered talismans go.[/b] Covered means a talisman you keep has every one of its skills at the same or a higher level, and slots that hold everything its slots can (weapon and armor slots compared separately). Of identical copies the cheaper one stays.
[*][b]Every skill gets a ranking[/b] of the talismans that have it: higher level of that skill, then bigger slots in total, then more slots, then more weapon slots, then stronger other skills (each counted against the best level of that skill in your box), then the cheaper talisman. [b]The top N of every skill stay.[/b]
[*][b]Every slot shape gets a ranking too[/b] (A3, A2 A1, W1 A1 A1, ...): the talismans that can hold it, by the strength of all their skills, then their slots. [b]The top N of every slot shape stay.[/b]
[*][b]The rest is sold[/b] if it is unique and within your rarity limit, unless it has a skill set to Keep all.
[/list]
[b]Per skill[/b] (Skills panel): Default, its own Best 1/2/3/5/10, Keep all (from a level), or Don't care. Don't care leaves the skill out of every comparison; if that would remove your best level of it, the summary warns in yellow and the confirmation lists it in red.
[b]Example: the 11 talismans with Poison Resistance in a real box, in ranking order[/b]
[code]
 #  Talisman                                                  Slots     Best 10  Best 5  Best 3
 1  R8 Attack Boost 3, Poison Resistance 3                    W1 A1 A1  Keep     Keep    Keep
 2  R7 Critical Eye 3, Poison Resistance 3                    A1 A1     Keep     Keep    Keep
 3  R7 Poison Attack 3, Poison Resistance 3                   A1 A1     Keep     Keep    Keep
 4  R7 Blast Attack 3, Poison Resistance 3                    A1        Keep     Keep    Sell
 5  R6 Focus 2, Poison Resistance 2, Survival Expert 2        A2 A1     Keep     Keep    Sell
 6  R7 Attack Boost 3, Poison Resistance 2, Divine Blessing 1 A1 A1     Keep     Sell    Sell
 7  R7 Sleep Attack 3, Poison Resistance 2, Intimidator 1     A2        Keep     Sell    Sell
 8  R6 Exhaust Func. 1, Resentment 1, Poison Resistance 2     A1        Keep     Sell    Sell
 9  R8 Critical Eye 3, Counterstrike 1, Poison Resistance 1   W1 A1     Keep     Sell    Sell
10  R7 Critical Status 3, Wide-Range 3, Poison Resistance 1   A2        Keep     Sell    Sell
11  R7 Spread/Power Shots 1, Maximum Might 1, Poison Resist. 1 A2       Keep*    Sell    Sell
[/code]
Level 3 comes before level 2; at the same level, bigger slots win (1 beats 2-4 with W1 A1 A1), then more slots (6 beats 7), then stronger other skills (10 beats 11). * Number 11 is outside the top 10 for Poison Resistance but number 6 for Spread/Power Shots, so best 10 keeps it for that skill. A talisman is only sold when it is outside the top N for [b]every[/b] one of its skills and for its slot shape. With best 3, your three Poison Resistance 3 talismans with the most slots stay, so Poison Resistance 3 never leaves your box.

So the number 1 of every skill and every slot shape always stays: [b]your best level of every skill never goes down[/b], and rare skills (on fewer than N talismans) stay. A good talisman can still be sold when better ones exist for every one of its skills; its Why text shows how close it came, for example "Not in your best 3 · closest Item Prolonger #10 of 12". Kept rows say why they stay: "Ambush #1 of 21", "Slot shape A3 #2 of 18". A smaller N sells more; selling in steps (best 10, then 5, then 3) lets you check the list each time.

Every Keep option shows how many talismans it sells and for how much before you choose it. Every row says why: "Same as #1032 (kept)", "Covered by #875 …", "Not in your best 3 · closest Item Prolonger #10 of 12", "Ambush #1 of 21". You get the game's own price (1,500 / 3,000 / 4,500 / 8,000 z for rarity 5 / 6 / 7 / 8). Every run writes a JSON receipt.

[size=4][b]Tools[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Stars[/b]: give every kept talisman (or your Keep picks) the game's own favorite star, which Bulk Sell and other mods never sell, and remove exactly the stars Bulk Sell added. Your own stars are never touched.
[*][b]Export[/b]: copy your talismans for [url=https://mhwilds.wiki-db.com/sim/?hl=en]mhwilds.wiki-db.com[/url] (Talisman tab > Import/Export Charms; importing replaces the site's list), or save a CSV. All talismans, what stays, or only the sales; names in the game's language or in English, Japanese, Korean or Chinese.
[*][b]Melding Pot points[/b] of the planned sales next to their zenny.
[*][b]Auto-clean watch[/b] (off by default): while the REFramework menu is closed, a message on the right of the screen, in the style of the game's own notices, tells you when new items arrive or the box is almost full; the [b]New arrivals[/b] filter then lists the new talismans. It never sells without your click.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Never sold[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The equipped talisman, and talismans used in any loadout
[*]Favorites
[*]Talismans with decorations attached
[*]Crafted talismans
[*]Talismans with an RNG Charm Crafting Set/Group bonus
[/list]
A confirmation only sells the list it showed. Unique talismans need an extra tick, and anything you would lose is listed in red and needs its own tick. The list is scanned again whenever the box may have changed, each talisman is checked again right before it is sold, and an independent check holds back any sale that does not prove itself. Selling waits while a game menu is open or the game is saving, and stops on its own if zenny does not go up by exactly the expected amount. If something cannot be checked (a game update, an unreadable RNG Charm Crafting file), selling turns off and says why.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]REFramework (a recent nightly build is recommended)
[*]Tested on Steam build 24705561 (October 2026)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Fluffy Mod Manager[/b]: import the zip without unpacking it, then enable [i]Bulk Sell Equipment[/i].
[b]Manual[/b]: copy the [i]reframework[/i] folder from the zip into the game folder (next to MonsterHunterWilds.exe).

[size=4][b]How to use[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Stand in the field or at camp with no game menu open, then press [b]Insert[/b].
[*]Open [b]Script Generated UI > Bulk Sell Equipment > Show window[/b].
[*]Click [b]Scan Equipment Box[/b], choose a [b]Keep[/b] option and review the list.
[*]Optionally, click [b]Sell just 1 (test)[/b] first. Then click [b]Sell N talismans[/b], tick what the confirmation asks for, and [b]Yes, sell[/b].
[*]Let the game autosave, for example by fast travelling.
[/list]
[b]Sales cannot be undone and the game has no buyback. Back up your save first.[/b] To free a lot of space, sell in steps (best 10, then 5, then 3). Sales are written to disk at the game's next autosave. If you close the game before then, they are not kept.

[size=4][b]Updating from 0.2.x[/b][/size]
Your settings are converted once (the old file stays as [i]config.v1.json[/i]), and the window says what changed. The rarity rule becomes "Keep the best 1 per skill" up to that rarity.

[size=4][b]Files[/b][/size]
Settings: [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/config.json[/i]
Your ticks: [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/picks/[/i]
Stars Bulk Sell added: [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/stars/[/i]
Exports: [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/export/[/i]
Box contents at the last scan (for new arrivals): [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/seen/[/i]
Receipts: [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/receipts/[/i]

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Crafted talismans are not used when deciding what is covered.
[*]Decorations you could still slot in are not counted. Decoration-aware comparison is planned.
[*]"Best N" ranks by skill level and slots only; use the Skills panel to say which skills matter to you.
[*]The interface is in English. Skill names follow your game language.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Source and bug reports[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/zamcoder/bulk-sell-equipment-mhwilds]github.com/zamcoder/bulk-sell-equipment-mhwilds[/url]
When reporting a bug, please attach your receipt file and the REFramework log ([i]re2_framework_log.txt[/i] in the game folder). For a wrong verdict, tick [b]Write debug files[/b] in the Bulk Sell menu, scan again, and attach the newest file from [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/debug/[/i].

